      "index": 7,
      "title": "Monogamish",
      "description": "<h2 style=\"text-align:center\"><strong><em>Mostly us,</em></strong><em> with the occasional spark.</em></h2><hr /><h2 style=\"text-align:center\"><strong>This is you if:</strong></h2><p data-rep=\"true\" style=\"text-align:justify\">You're a committed, <strong>monogamous-<em>feeling</em> couple</strong> who just <strong>doesn't want </strong>the all-or-nothing pressure a rare kiss on a trip, a birthday threesome, a specific agreed exception now and then.</p><p data-rep=\"true\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><strong>You're each other's person, </strong>full stop. You just like knowing the door isn't bolted shut. It's a valve, not a lifestyle small, contained openings that add spark without changing who you fundamentally are.</p><p data-rep=\"true\" style=\"text-align:justify\">The lowest-stakes way to be a <strong>little bit open.</strong></p><hr /><p data-rep=\"true\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><strong>Your customized Get Started pathway</strong></p><p data-rep=\"true\" style=\"text-align:justify\">keeps it simple:</p><ul style=\"text-align:center\"><li><p data-rep=\"true\" style=\"text-align:justify\">how to define your \"exceptions\" so they add spark (not confusion),</p></li><li><p data-rep=\"true\" style=\"text-align:justify\">when you might need an app (sometimes you don't),</p></li><li><p data-rep=\"true\" style=\"text-align:justify\">how to explore with the perfect amount of stretch,</p></li><li><p data-rep=\"true\" style=\"text-align:justify\">how to keep it special, agreed upon, and fun.</p></li></ul><p data-rep=\"true\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><em>Inside the guide.</em></p>",
